  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 237 PM EDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\n- Rain Mid-Week then Cooler\n\nShowers are moving off to the east of Lower Michigan on Sunday\nafternoon, but a thin deck of stratocu remains. Upper ridging with\nfair and warm weather continues into Monday before a shortwave \ntrough rides over the top of the ridge with a low pressure center\ntracking across the central Great Lakes on Tuesday. Showers are\npossible in an area of warm advection Monday night into Tuesday\nbut the steadier rain associated with an area of frontogenesis\nappears to move across northern Lower Michigan.\n\nAnother chance for rain comes on late Tuesday and early Wednesday\nacross the southern forecast area as a trailing cold front moves \nthrough and stalls. This is followed by another low moving along \nthe front and bringing rain on Thursday. Cooler air moves in as an\nupper trough digs across the eastern CONUS by the end of the \nweek.",
